messages.thinking:
`with_automatic_pagination` wraps cards in `turbo-frame id="#{name}-pagination-contents-#{page}"` with `class "display-contents"`? `pagination_list` div with class "#{name} display-contents" inside `.cards__list`; then `pagination_frame_tag` turbo-frame. So direct children of `.cards__list` are NOT `article.card`; they're nested inside `.display-contents` div / turbo-frame! Our selector `:scope > article.card` finds none, so `#insertionPointFor` returns null => append card at END. That explains [text, layout] (text existing first, layout appended). Great catch.

Also means our card move logic needs to insert into the proper container matching actual structure. Cards are nested:
`.cards__list` > `div[id=...-pagination-list].display-contents` > `turbo-frame[id=...-pagination-contents-N] > article.card`
